<%- include('partials/header') %>

<div class="container py-5 legal-page">
  <div class="row justify-content-center">
    <div class="col-lg-8">
      <h1 class="mb-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-muted">Last updated: October 2026</p>

      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how Sunrise Public School ("the School", "we") collects, uses,
        stores and shares personal information through this website and student portal
        (together, "the Portal"). By using the Portal, you agree to the practices described below.
        If you do not agree, do not use the Portal.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
      <p>We collect the following categories of information:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Student personal data:</strong> full name, date of birth, gender, class and section,
          admission date, address, blood group, photograph (if provided), parent name and phone number,
          guardian name and phone number, and email address.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Academic data:</strong> exam marks, grades, subject-wise performance and class rank.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Financial data:</strong> fee structure, payment amounts, payment dates, payment mode,
          receipt numbers and outstanding balances.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Transport data:</strong> bus route, stops, pickup point and transport fee records.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Activity enrollments:</strong> sports, dance, music, art and similar programs,
          including associated fees.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Complaints:</strong> titles, descriptions, categories, status and administrative
          responses submitted through the Portal.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Account data:</strong> username (student ID or staff username), password (stored only
          as a bcrypt hash; we never store or display plain-text passwords) and session records.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. How we use this information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To maintain accurate student admission and contact records.</li>
        <li>To assess, record and display academic performance.</li>
        <li>To calculate fees, record payments and issue receipts.</li>
        <li>To administer transport routes and activity enrollments.</li>
        <li>To receive, respond to and resolve complaints.</li>
        <li>To authenticate users and restrict access to the correct portal and the correct student's own data.</li>
        <li>To meet legal and regulatory obligations applicable to schools.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Who can access this information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Administrators and authorized staff</strong> can access records of all students for
          legitimate school administration purposes.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Students</strong> can access only their own record, using their unique student ID and password.
          A student cannot view another student's data.
        </li>
        <li>
          We do not sell, rent or trade personal information to advertisers, data brokers or any third party.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Data retention</h2>
      <p>
        Student records are retained for the duration of the student's enrollment and for any further
        period required by applicable education regulations and record-keeping obligations.
        When retention is no longer required, records are deleted or destroyed securely.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Data security</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Passwords are stored as bcrypt hashes and are never displayed in plain text.</li>
        <li>Access to the Portal requires authentication; sessions expire after a period of inactivity.</li>
        <li>Student data is transmitted over HTTPS when the site is served on a secure domain.</li>
        <li>Access is role-based: students see only their own data; staff access is limited to authorized accounts.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        The Portal uses a session cookie to keep you signed in. This cookie is strictly necessary for the
        Portal to function and is not used for advertising or cross-site tracking.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Parents and guardians</h2>
      <p>
        For students in Nursery through Class 8, the parent or legal guardian is the primary contact and
        may exercise any right described in this policy on behalf of the student by contacting the School office.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
      <p>You have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Request access to the personal data held about you or your ward.</li>
        <li>Request correction of inaccurate or incomplete data.</li>
        <li>Raise objections to the processing of your data, subject to legal requirements.</li>
        <li>Lodge a complaint with the School or with the relevant data protection authority.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The "Last updated" date at the top of this page
        reflects the most recent revision. Continued use of the Portal after changes constitutes acceptance
        of the revised policy.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Contact</h2>
      <p>
